ng images  instead of you know or looking at a  frame by frame within a large set of  images as opposed to a single image but  it effectively functions the same way in  terms of the label objects face  detection that sort of thing but your  back to you right is it worth the  investment to stream that data do you  need to have the network bandwidth you  need to have a more capable device on  primer in the store to actually send  that data up it might not be right  depending on the the size and the scope  of the Diploma you're trying to put  together it might not be appropriate fit  well what about shelf based inventory  right how do we see all the way through  the back of a shelf we could with shelf  mounted cameras and it's actually a  great partner of ours tracks who's over  in the retail showcased in Moscone West  actually has shelf based cameras exactly  for this purpose so they've actually got  a really cool demo of stacks of a box of  stacks of boxes of donuts and every time  you pull a doughnut out it updates the  inventory count so that actually could  work for certain other use cases where  again there's sort of narrowly kind of  packed in items you can't get overhead  cameras and appropriately they've got a  good little shelf based system and it  functions in a lot of similar ways to  what I've shown you today what about a  custom model what if you want to go with  something that we can't do with vision  API or auto ml what if you need  something incredibly more specific well  that's where you can use something like  tensorflow  to build a very specific custom object  detection model and you actually run  that on top of our cloud ml engine  service and so what the cloud management  service gives you  is the ability to train an incredible  scale and do things like hyper parameter  tuning which lets you specify which  parameters in your model do you want to  tweak and how many permutations do you  want us to run them through so we can  actually take your mode